                <pb facs="0459" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.011/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-18T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                                1920—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 19—8:55
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>18. New Constitution proclaimed this afternoon with elaborate ceremonies and
                    military display. Perfect order prevailed. To-morrow declared national
                    holiday.</p>
                <p>In view of good feeling between Peru and United States at this time I
                    respectfully suggest that recognition as <hi rendition="#italic">de jure</hi>
                    Government be extended as soon as deemed expedient.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
